<title>ITALY: Italy's Bologna sees Feb CPI at -0.2 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Bologna sees Feb CPI at -0.2 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>BOLOGNA, Italy 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Bologna said its February consumer price index stood at -0.2 percent month-on-month and 2.4 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In January, Bologna's inflation rate was 0.3 and 2.9 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Bologna is one of 11 Italian cities which published inflation data Thursday and Friday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 7.62 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to January 1997):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		    -0.2   (0.3)     2.4  (2.9)</p>
<p>    Food				 -0.1  (-0.3)     0.0  (0.8)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.0   (0.0)     2.5  (2.5)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges  -1.6   (0.6)     5.0  (6.7)</p>
<p>    Furniture			  -0.4   (0.0)     1.2  (1.7)</p>
<p>    Health services		   1.3   (2.6)     5.8  (4.5)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.3  (-0.8)     1.9  (2.9)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture    -1.1   (0.7)     5.8  (7.3)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.4   (0.0)     2.7  (2.3)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.3   (0.6)     2.3  (2.0)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.2   (0.8)     1.2  (1.1)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
